  "answer_for_xiao_man": "When routing cues stay honest, artifact-shape routing matches fixed task-type depth on catch — shape is a schema proxy, not a failure-signal cascade. Cue erasure (strip budget cue, wrong fingerprint residual): fixed=100% vs shape=82% — depth cues are load-bearing. Decoy nesting on T2: fixed catch=100% (5.1 ops) vs shape catch=0% (24.0 ops) — misroute, not just waste. Answer fork: artifact characteristics can set P-level *if they encode schema depth and are not agent-writable escape hatches*. That is still matched-depth routing, not 'cheap pre-check on P1/P2 fail'."
